{
 "section_summary": "The section finishes an economic survey of Japanese-occupied Asia, covering policy in occupied China, resource development, overseas Chinese communities, machinery shortages, and rail transport. It then contains a Chungking Embassy despatch dated July 13, 1943, with a contents list and an enclosure of economic reports drawn from Japanese and puppet-regime broadcasts. The enclosure, which continues beyond page 220, covers industrial mobilization in Japan and developments across occupied East and Southeast Asia.",
